\cf0 # Last Word Standing \'97 Dev Workflow\
\
## LINKS\
\
Production:\
https://www.reddit.com/r/lastwordstanding/\
\
Development:\
https://www.reddit.com/r/lastwordstanding_dev/\
\
Playtest:\
https://www.reddit.com/r/lastwordstanding_dev/?playtest=lastwordstanding\
\
Versions / Review:\
https://developers.reddit.com/apps/lastwordstanding/app-versions\
\
\
# DEVELOP\
\
Open project in VS Code.\
\
Run:\
\
npm run dev\
\
Then open the Playtest URL above.\
\
Leave `npm run dev` running while working.\
Saving files automatically rebuilds/updates Playtest.\
\
When finished:\
\
Ctrl+C\
\
\
# COMING BACK AFTER A LONG BREAK\
\
Check Devvit:\
\
npx devvit --version\
\
If Devvit is outdated:\
\
npm install --save-dev devvit@latest\
npx devvit update app\
\
Then:\
\
npm run dev\
\
IMPORTANT: Make sure the existing game works before changing anything.\
\
\
# RELEASE\
\
1. Test everything in Playtest.\
\
2. Stop development:\
   Ctrl+C\
\
3. Confirm Reddit account:\
   npx devvit whoami\
\
4. Submit new version for review:\
   npx devvit publish\
\
5. Check review status:\
   https://developers.reddit.com/apps/lastwordstanding/app-versions\
\
6. Once APPROVED, update production:\
   npx devvit install lastwordstanding\
\
7. Open r/lastwordstanding and verify the new version works.\
\
\
# REMEMBER\
\
npm run dev\
= develop + Playtest\
\
npx devvit publish\
= submit a new version for Reddit review\
\
npx devvit install lastwordstanding\
= put latest approved version on production\
\
0.1.7.xxx\
= Playtest\
\
0.1.8\
= released version}